## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** GPT-5.4 nano — "our cheapest GPT-5.4-class model for simple high-volume tasks" (official model docs tagline: classification, data extraction, ranking, sub-agents).
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API — Responses API + Chat Completions + Batch supported (Realtime/Assistants not supported). Default snapshot `gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Snapshot dated 2026-03-17; knowledge cutoff Aug 31, 2025 (official model docs).
- **IDs:** `openai/gpt-5.4-nano` (snapshot `gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17`). No Free ID exists on OpenCode Zen.
- **Context window:** 400,000 total; 272,000 max input; 128,000 max output (official model docs). Reasoning token support; effort none/low/medium/high/xhigh (default `none`).
- **Modalities:** Text + image in; text out. Tools (Responses API): function_calling, web_search, file_search, image_generation, code_interpreter, hosted_shell, apply_patch, skills, mcp (no tool_search/computer_use, unlike GPT-5.4 Mini).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-01):** $0.20 / $1.25 per MTok (input/output); cached input $0.02; +10% on regional-processing endpoints (official model docs pricing table).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary nano variant of the GPT-5.4 family; parameter count undisclosed.

